<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasir Jung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1712">1712</a>–<a href="/years/1750">1750</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasir Jung was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-jah-i">Asaf Jah I</a> who succeeded his father as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a> in 1748. Backed by the British, he fought the claims of his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaffar-jung">Muzaffar Jung</a> and the French in the Carnatic. He was killed in December 1750 by one of his own Pathan allies during a battle with the French.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nasir-jung.jpg" alt="Nasir Jung" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hyderabad, India (made) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasir_Jung,_Nizam_of_Hyderabad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
